- Blocker: mixed primary/fallback captures can reorder images. In `apps/scraper/scrapers/actions/handlers/image.py:385-404`, request-API successes are appended to `results` immediately, while fallback candidates are appended after the fallback batch. For input `[A, B]` where A needs fallback and B succeeds via request, the returned metadata/final image list becomes `[B, A]`. Product image order is significant because the first image is commonly treated as the primary image, and current tests only cover single-image fallback or all-primary success. Preserve original indices, e.g. preallocate result slots and fill fallback results back into their original positions, and add a mixed two-image regression test.
- Blocker: the production retry worker gap is accurate. A repository search excluding tests finds no production `new ImageRetryProcessor(...)` or `pollAndProcess(...)` caller; only `apps/web/lib/scraper-callback/image-retry-processor.ts:440-443` defines polling. Also, a default instantiation would still fail capture because the constructor uses `defaultCaptureImage` when no capture client is supplied (`apps/web/lib/scraper-callback/image-retry-processor.ts:429-433`), and that default throws (`apps/web/lib/scraper-callback/image-retry-processor.ts:532-534`). As implemented, code can enqueue `image_retry_queue` rows, but no production path consumes them.
- Note: the backfill script’s local config loader drops the top-level `requires_login` field before passing configs into the shared helper (`apps/web/scripts/backfill-login-protected-images-logic.ts:131-137`), so the helper’s explicit `requires_login === true` branch (`apps/web/lib/scraper-config-login.ts:10-12`) is ineffective for configs loaded through `runLoginProtectedImageBackfill`. Existing local login configs also have login/workflow markers, so this may not break current PetFoodEx/Phillips/Orgill detection, but it leaves a coverage gap and contradicts the stated shared-helper behavior. Include `requires_login: parsed.requires_login` and add a backfill-loader or `resolveLoginProtectedScraperSlugs` fixture test for a config with only `requires_login: true`.
- Note: admin retry updates change existing rows to `auth_401` but do not reset `retry_count` or normalize `max_retries` (`apps/web/app/api/admin/scraping/retry-image/route.ts:61-70`). The pending RPC only returns rows where `retry_count < max_retries` (`apps/web/supabase/migrations/20260327192421_ensure_image_retry_queue_schema_uses_sku.sql:107-109`), so an exhausted existing entry can remain unprocessed even after manual requeue. Consider resetting `retry_count` to 0 and setting `max_retries` consistently with auth retries when manually retrying.
